Mavergreen's own, not yet upstream: clang reads a value caught by value at no more than the target's
exception object alignment. clang (22.1.8, and main as of 2026-10-19) reads it at the type's own.

Why: before macOS 10.14, libc++abi places a thrown object 8 bytes past a 16-byte boundary, and clang
knows it: getExnObjectAlignment() is 8 bytes there, and the throw side (emitThrow) uses it. The catch
side did not. InitCatchParam read a caught scalar with MakeNaturalAlignAddrLValue and copied a caught
class at getClassPointerAlignment, both the type's own alignment, so catching an __int128 or a
16-byte-aligned class by value emitted an aligned SSE load that faulted on 10.9 to 10.13. Both reads now
assume the smaller of the type's alignment and the exception object's. Modern targets, whose exception
objects are 16-byte aligned, are unchanged.

Not covered, and not fixable here: catching such a type by reference, which binds to the exception
object itself, so every use of the reference assumes the type's alignment.

tests/catch-align-test.sh is the regression test (the IR on any host, with a 10.14 control; run where
x86_64 runs, which on 10.9 is CI's on-mavericks job). To offer upstream, with a clang CodeGen lit test of
the same IR.

diff --git a/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp
index 63cb4b6..c907695 100644
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/ItaniumCXXABI.cpp
@@ -5025,9 +5025,13 @@ static void InitCatchParam(CodeGenFunction &CGF,
       llvm_unreachable("bad ownership qualifier!");
     }
 
-    // Otherwise, it returns a pointer into the exception object.
-
-    LValue srcLV = CGF.MakeNaturalAlignAddrLValue(AdjustedExn, CatchType);
+    // Otherwise, it returns a pointer into the exception object, which is
+    // aligned to no more than the target's exception object alignment (8 bytes
+    // before macOS 10.14, whatever the type's own).
+    CharUnits SrcAlign =
+        std::min(CGF.CGM.getNaturalTypeAlignment(CatchType),
+                 CGF.getContext().getExnObjectAlignment());
+    LValue srcLV = CGF.MakeAddrLValue(AdjustedExn, CatchType, SrcAlign);
     LValue destLV = CGF.MakeAddrLValue(ParamAddr, CatchType);
     switch (TEK) {
     case TEK_Complex:
@@ -5047,7 +5051,11 @@ static void InitCatchParam(CodeGenFunction &CGF,
 
   assert(isa<RecordType>(CatchType) && "unexpected catch type!");
   auto catchRD = CatchType->getAsCXXRecordDecl();
-  CharUnits caughtExnAlignment = CGF.CGM.getClassPointerAlignment(catchRD);
+  // The exception object is aligned to no more than the target's exception
+  // object alignment, whatever the class's own (see the scalar case above).
+  CharUnits caughtExnAlignment =
+      std::min(CGF.CGM.getClassPointerAlignment(catchRD),
+               CGF.getContext().getExnObjectAlignment());
 
   llvm::Type *PtrTy = CGF.DefaultPtrTy;
 
